From: vincenzopio <43883474+vincenzopio@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 02:07:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] service: install the game for the launcher.

LAUNCHER_INSTALL takes a game's Store ID, a market and a staging folder of the launcher, and
answers with InstallUpdate frames: the progress of the download and of the extraction, then the
installed version or a failure. Closing the channel stops the install with the service, and the
next INSTALL goes on with what was downloaded. The channel's protocol is now 2.

The content's key comes first, so that a user who does not own the game downloads nothing. The
CDNs serve the package over plain HTTP with no hash to check it against, and Microsoft signs its
header with a key nobody else has. Every page is therefore checked against the package's own hash
tree as it arrives, which catches damage but not a package made to pass. A download resumes from
the last page that checks, from any CDN, with limited retries.

The game is extracted into the staging folder's game, with paths that stay inside it. The files
the package keeps encrypted on disk, such as the executable, are decrypted with the others, and
every program must start with MZ, which also catches a wrong key. New failures: NO_SPACE with the
bytes needed, DAMAGED, UNREADABLE_PACKAGE and DISK. The service's client for Microsoft's services
is now HTTPS only; the downloads have their own.

Original work for macrock (GPL-3.0-only, as Xodus).

Topic: install
